  "preamble": "The transformation from a voiced postalveolar affricate ([d͡ʒ]) to a voiceless alveolar fricative ([s]) combines devoicing, deaffrication and fronting. It is attested in the Chamic languages of mainland Southeast Asia, where Proto-Chamic *j became s in Tsat (Hainan) and in Jarai.",
